# h264_inter — inter prediction for the H.264 decoder: the motion
# vectors of clause 8.4.1 (`h264_mvpred`, in the token stream) and the
# prediction samples of clause 8.4.2 (`h264_inter`, behind an SDRAM
# burst port, through a reference cache).
#
# Written from ITU-T H.264 (06/2026) and nothing else. `README.md` says
# what is checked bit for bit and against what, what the reference cache
# saves on real 720p streams, and what is not done yet (B slices, weighted
# prediction, the SDRAM agent's `frame_addr`).
#
# `h264_mvpred` is the other block of the package; it has no SDRAM and
# sits between `h264_parse` and `h264_recon`. Its ports are in its own
# header.
name h264_inter
version 0.1.0
license MIT
description "H.264 inter prediction: motion vector prediction in the token stream, and quarter-sample luma / eighth-sample chroma motion compensation from tiled SDRAM through a sector cache; bit-exact against an independent decoder's dumps"

top h264_inter
target xc7

source rtl/h264_frame_addr_stub.v
source rtl/h264_inter.v
source rtl/h264_mvpred.v

port clk in
port rst_n in
port tok in 32
port tok_valid in
port tok_ready out
port map_frames in 64
port map_valid in
port map_ready out
port cmd_valid out
port cmd_ready in
port cmd_we out
port cmd_addr out 24
port cmd_len out 4
port wr_valid out
port wr_ready in
port wr_data out 16
port wr_be out 2
port rd_valid in
port rd_data in 16
port rd_last in
port pred_data out 32
port pred_valid out
port pred_ready in
